  "rationale": "The batch contains the continuation “A day with Ben,” but the period rule for any context ending in a noun has very large weight, overwhelming the observed preposition with after “A day.” Reduce that broad punctuation preference and add moderate support for a preposition after a determiner–noun ending. Add support for the observed opening determiner and following noun, and for paragraph boundaries after the opening companion phrase and after the sentence in that opener; the latter is deliberately conditioned on the wider visible structure so it does not make every noun-final period a paragraph break, which would conflict with replay examples. The phrase “Long ago,” also gives a reusable local cue for ago and the following comma. These are provisional generalizations from one document: other continuations after a noun or after “Long” remain possible, and other paragraph-boundary contexts may differ. The replay gate has not been evaluated.",
